{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ElevenLabs adapter is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"voice-focused"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It exposes five capabilities:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime voice agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtime"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtimeToken"},{"type":"text","value":") — full-duplex voice-to-voice conversations powered by ElevenLabs Conversational AI agents."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-speech"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":") — one-shot speech generation via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Music & sound effects"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsAudio"},{"type":"text","value":") — one-shot audio generation via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateAudio()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":") — speech-to-text via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice design"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsVoiceDesign"},{"type":"text","value":"): create a new voice via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It does not support text "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize()"},{"type":"text","value":" — use OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini for those."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The realtime adapter uses an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"agent-based architecture"}]},{"type":"text","value":" where you configure your conversational AI agent in the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://elevenlabs.io/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs dashboard"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (voice, personality, knowledge base, tools) and then connect to it at runtime. The adapter wraps the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@elevenlabs/client"},{"type":"text","value":" SDK for seamless integration with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Peer dependencies:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server generates a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"signed WebSocket URL"}]},{"type":"text","value":" so your API key never reaches the client. The signed URL is valid for 30 minutes."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\n// In your API route (Express, Hono, TanStack Start, etc.)\nexport async function POST() {\n  const token = await realtimeToken({\n    adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n      agentId: process.env.ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID!,\n    }),\n  })\n\n  return Response.json(token)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=elevenlabs-1"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"with-overrides","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With Overrides"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can override agent settings at token generation time without changing your dashboard configuration:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n    agentId: process.env.ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID!,\n    overrides: {\n      voiceId: 'custom-voice-id',\n      systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful voice assistant.',\n      firstMessage: 'Hello! How can I help you today?',\n      language: 'en',\n    },\n  }),\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=elevenlabs-1"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Setup"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"react-userealtimechat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React (useRealtimeChat)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nfunction VoiceChat() {\n  const {\n    status,\n    mode,\n    messages,\n    connect,\n    disconnect,\n    pendingUserTranscript,\n    pendingAssistantTranscript,\n    inputLevel,\n    outputLevel,\n  } = useRealtimeChat({\n    getToken: () =>\n      fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n    adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Status: {status}</p>\n      <p>Mode: {mode}</p>\n      <button onClick={status === 'idle' ? connect : disconnect}>\n        {status === 'idle' ? 'Start Conversation' : 'End Conversation'}\n      </button>\n      {pendingUserTranscript && <p>You: {pendingUserTranscript}...</p>}\n      {pendingAssistantTranscript && (\n        <p>AI: {pendingAssistantTranscript}...</p>\n      )}\n      {messages.map((msg) => (\n        <div key={msg.id}>\n          <strong>{msg.role}:</strong>\n          {msg.parts.map((part, i) => (\n            <span key={i}>\n              {part.type === 'text' ? part.content : null}\n              {part.type === 'audio' ? part.transcript : null}\n            </span>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"non-react-realtimeclient","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Non-React (RealtimeClient)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { RealtimeClient } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst client = new RealtimeClient({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  onMessage: (message) => {\n    console.log(`${message.role}:`, message.parts)\n  },\n  onStatusChange: (status) => {\n    console.log('Status:', status)\n  },\n  onModeChange: (mode) => {\n    console.log('Mode:', mode)\n  },\n})\n\nawait client.connect()","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs supports client-side tools that execute in the browser. Define tools using the standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" API:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Get weather for a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    conditions: z.string(),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.client(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/weather?location=${location}`)\n  return res.json()\n})\n\n// Pass tools to the hook\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool results are automatically serialized to strings and returned to the ElevenLabs agent. The adapter converts TanStack tool definitions into the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@elevenlabs/client"},{"type":"text","value":" clientTools format internally."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsrealtimetoken-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtimeToken"},{"type":"text","value":" Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Used on the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to generate a signed WebSocket URL."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agentId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent ID configured in the ElevenLabs dashboard. *Falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID"},{"type":"text","value":"; required only if that env var is unset"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overrides.voiceId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom voice ID to override the agent's default voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overrides.systemPrompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom system prompt to override the agent's default"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overrides.firstMessage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First message the agent speaks when the session starts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overrides.language"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language code (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'en'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'es'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'fr'"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsrealtime-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtime"},{"type":"text","value":" Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Used on the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to establish the connection."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connectionMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'websocket' | 'webrtc'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"auto-detect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transport protocol for the connection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | DebugConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable debug logging — pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for all categories, or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DebugConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" to select categories/sink"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"differences-from-openai-realtime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Differences from OpenAI Realtime"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs and OpenAI take different approaches to realtime voice:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent-based. Configure voice, personality, and knowledge in the ElevenLabs dashboard or via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overrides"},{"type":"text","value":" at token time."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session-based. Configure "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", etc. per session via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat"},{"type":"text","value":" options."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Token type"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signed WebSocket URL (valid 30 minutes)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ephemeral API token (valid ~10 minutes)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transport"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebSocket (default) or WebRTC"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebRTC"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio handling"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@elevenlabs/client"},{"type":"text","value":" SDK manages audio capture and playback automatically"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI manages WebRTC peer connection and audio tracks"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"VAD"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handled by ElevenLabs server-side"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"semantic"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manual"},{"type":"text","value":" modes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime updates"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session config is set at creation time and cannot be changed mid-session"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateSession()"},{"type":"text","value":" for mid-session config changes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image input"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not supported"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendImage()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time domain data"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not available from the SDK"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available for waveform visualizations"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"audio-visualization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio Visualization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ElevenLabs adapter provides audio visualization data through the same interface as other realtime adapters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst {\n  inputLevel, // 0-1 normalized microphone volume\n  outputLevel, // 0-1 normalized speaker volume\n  getInputFrequencyData, // Uint8Array frequency spectrum\n  getOutputFrequencyData,\n} = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ElevenLabs provides volume levels and frequency data but does not expose time-domain data. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getInputTimeDomainData()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getOutputTimeDomainData()"},{"type":"text","value":" methods return static placeholder arrays. The default audio sample rate is 16kHz."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set these in your server environment:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-elevenlabs-api-key\nELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=your-agent-id","lang":"bash"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ELEVENLABS_API_KEY"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your ElevenLabs API key, used server-side for generating signed URLs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default agent ID. Can also be passed directly to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtimeToken()"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get your API key from the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://elevenlabs.io/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs dashboard"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Create and configure agents in the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conversational AI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" section of the dashboard."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For one-shot speech generation (not realtime), use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":" option supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mp3"},{"type":"text","value":" (default), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pcm"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opus"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wav"},{"type":"text","value":". WAV output contains 44.1 kHz, 16-bit mono PCM with a RIFF header. Requests for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aac"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flac"},{"type":"text","value":" throw before the API call. An explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.outputFormat"},{"type":"text","value":" overrides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":" and returns the selected provider format without WAV wrapping."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  text: \"Hello from ElevenLabs!\",\n  voice: \"Rachel\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.audio); // Base64-encoded audio","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dialogue-and-timings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dialogue and timings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs has a separate dialogue endpoint that takes up to "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10 distinct\nvoices"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and a timestamped twin of each endpoint. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamps"},{"type":"text","value":"\npick between them, so you never choose an endpoint by hand:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  turns: [\n    { text: \"Knock knock.\", voice: \"bYTqZQo3Jz7LQtmGTgwi\" },\n    { text: \"Who is there?\", voice: \"6lCwbsX1yVjD49QmpkTR\" },\n  ],\n  timestamps: true,\n});\n\n// Character timings for the whole clip.\nconsole.log(result.alignment?.unit); // 'character'\n\n// One entry per turn, with the voice that spoke it.\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.turnIndex, segment.voice, segment.text);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"segments"},{"type":"text","value":" only comes back from the dialogue endpoint. A single-voice request\nwith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamps: true"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alignment"},{"type":"text","value":" alone."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"music-sound-effects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Music & Sound Effects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsAudio"},{"type":"text","value":" covers both music generation and sound effects depending on the model:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateAudio } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsAudio } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\n// Music generation\nconst music = await generateAudio({\n  adapter: elevenlabsAudio(\"music_v2_5\"),\n  prompt: \"An upbeat synthwave track for a product launch\",\n});\n\n// Sound effects\nconst sfx = await generateAudio({\n  adapter: elevenlabsAudio(\"eleven_text_to_sound_v2\"),\n  prompt: \"A glass shattering on concrete\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"listing-voices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listing Voices"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" can read the account's voice catalog, which includes anything "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":" has saved:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { listVoices } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst { voices } = await listVoices({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  origins: [\"generated\", \"cloned\"],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs has no origin filter on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET /v1/voices"},{"type":"text","value":", so the adapter fetches the catalog and narrows in memory. Its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"famous"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"high_quality"},{"type":"text","value":" categories both read as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"professional"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"voice-design","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice Design"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsVoiceDesign"},{"type":"text","value":" creates a new voice from a description. The voice IDs it returns go straight into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVoice } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign(\"eleven_ttv_v3\"),\n  prompt: \"A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties with a slight Irish lilt\",\n  name: \"Irish Narrator\",\n});\n\nconst [voice] = result.voices;\nif (!voice) throw new Error(\"The provider returned no voices.\");\n\nconsole.log(voice.voiceId);\nconsole.log(voice.saved); // true, because a name was given","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", you get preview voices to audition. With a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", the best candidate is kept in your ElevenLabs voice library."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_ttv_v3"},{"type":"text","value":" also accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceAudio"},{"type":"text","value":", a clip of a real speaker used as a design reference — it still needs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.promptStrength"},{"type":"text","value":" balances the two. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_multilingual_ttv_v2"},{"type":"text","value":" takes no reference audio. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/voice-creation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice Creation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full guide."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Family"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-speech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_v4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_v4_turbo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_v3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_v3_conversational"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_multilingual_v2"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_flash_v2_5"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_flash_v2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Music"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"music_v2_5"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"music_v2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sound effects"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_text_to_sound_v2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scribe_v2"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scribe_v2_medical"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice design"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_ttv_v3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_multilingual_ttv_v2"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs deprecated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_turbo_v2"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_turbo_v2_5"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_monolingual_v1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scribe_v1"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"music_v1"},{"type":"text","value":". The adapter still accepts them, and each is commented as deprecated in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model-meta.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". Move to the current model in the same row."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"transcription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcribe audio with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: elevenlabsTranscription(\"scribe_v2\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behind-a-proxy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behind a proxy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":". These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createElevenLabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst adapter = createElevenLabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\", process.env.ELEVENLABS_API_KEY!, {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/elevenlabs\",\n  defaultHeaders: { \"cf-aig-authorization\": `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This applies to the speech, audio, and transcription adapters. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":" win."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsrealtimetoken-options-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtimeToken(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an ElevenLabs realtime token adapter for server-side use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"realtimeToken()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.agentId"},{"type":"text","value":" - Agent ID from the ElevenLabs dashboard"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.overrides?.voiceId"},{"type":"text","value":" - Custom voice ID"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.overrides?.systemPrompt"},{"type":"text","value":" - Custom system prompt"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.overrides?.firstMessage"},{"type":"text","value":" - First message the agent speaks"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.overrides?.language"},{"type":"text","value":" - Language code"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeTokenAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"realtimeToken()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsrealtime-options-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtime(options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an ElevenLabs realtime client adapter for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.connectionMode?"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'websocket'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'webrtc'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default: auto-detect)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.debug?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Enable debug logging"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsspeech-model-config-createelevenlabsspeech-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createElevenLabsSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an ElevenLabs text-to-speech adapter for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsaudio-model-config-createelevenlabsaudio-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsAudio(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createElevenLabsAudio(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an ElevenLabs audio adapter that covers both music generation and sound effects (selected via the model id) for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateAudio()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabstranscription-model-config-createelevenlabstranscription-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsTranscription(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createElevenLabsTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an ElevenLabs transcription adapter for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsvoicedesign-model-config-createelevenlabsvoicedesign-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsVoiceDesign(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createElevenLabsVoiceDesign(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an ElevenLabs voice-design adapter for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabsspeech-listvoices-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech(...).listVoices(options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the account's voice catalog via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET /v1/voices"},{"type":"text","value":", for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listVoices()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No text chat support"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Use OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or another text adapter for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No summarization"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Use a text adapter for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No image input"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (realtime) -- ElevenLabs realtime does not support sending images during a conversation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No runtime session updates"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (realtime) -- Session configuration is fixed at connection time."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No time-domain audio data"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (realtime) -- Frequency data and volume levels are available, but waveform data is not."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent required"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (realtime) -- You must create and configure an agent in the ElevenLabs dashboard before using the realtime adapter."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../media/realtime-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime Voice Chat Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Complete guide to building realtime voice applications"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Alternative realtime voice provider with WebRTC"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about the isomorphic tool system"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"server-setup","text":"Server Setup","level":2},{"id":"with-overrides","text":"With Overrides","level":3},{"id":"client-setup","text":"Client Setup","level":2},{"id":"react-userealtimechat","text":"React (useRealtimeChat)","level":3},{"id":"non-react-realtimeclient","text":"Non-React (RealtimeClient)","level":3},{"id":"client-tools","text":"Client Tools","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"elevenlabsrealtimetoken-options","text":"elevenlabsRealtimeToken Options","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabsrealtime-options","text":"elevenlabsRealtime Options","level":3},{"id":"differences-from-openai-realtime","text":"Differences from OpenAI Realtime","level":2},{"id":"audio-visualization","text":"Audio Visualization","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"text-to-speech","text":"Text-to-Speech","level":2},{"id":"dialogue-and-timings","text":"Dialogue and timings","level":3},{"id":"music-sound-effects","text":"Music & Sound Effects","level":2},{"id":"listing-voices","text":"Listing Voices","level":2},{"id":"voice-design","text":"Voice Design","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"transcription","text":"Transcription","level":2},{"id":"behind-a-proxy","text":"Behind a proxy","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"elevenlabsrealtimetoken-options-2","text":"elevenlabsRealtimeToken(options)","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabsrealtime-options-2","text":"elevenlabsRealtime(options?)","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabsspeech-model-config-createelevenlabsspeech-model-apikey-config","text":"elevenlabsSpeech(model, config?) / createElevenLabsSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabsaudio-model-config-createelevenlabsaudio-model-apikey-config","text":"elevenlabsAudio(model, config?) / createElevenLabsAudio(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabstranscription-model-config-createelevenlabstranscription-model-apikey-config","text":"elevenlabsTranscription(model, config?) / createElevenLabsTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabsvoicedesign-model-config-createelevenlabsvoicedesign-model-apikey-config","text":"elevenlabsVoiceDesign(model, config?) / createElevenLabsVoiceDesign(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabsspeech-listvoices-options","text":"elevenlabsSpeech(...).listVoices(options?)","level":3},{"id":"limitations","text":"Limitations","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe ElevenLabs adapter is **voice-focused**. It exposes five capabilities:\n\n- **Realtime voice agents** (`elevenlabsRealtime` / `elevenlabsRealtimeToken`) — full-duplex voice-to-voice conversations powered by ElevenLabs Conversational AI agents.\n- **Text-to-speech** (`elevenlabsSpeech`) — one-shot speech generation via `generateSpeech()`.\n- **Music & sound effects** (`elevenlabsAudio`) — one-shot audio generation via `generateAudio()`.\n- **Transcription** (`elevenlabsTranscription`) — speech-to-text via `generateTranscription()`.\n- **Voice design** (`elevenlabsVoiceDesign`): create a new voice via `generateVoice()`.\n\nIt does not support text `chat()` or `summarize()` — use OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini for those.\n\nThe realtime adapter uses an **agent-based architecture** where you configure your conversational AI agent in the [ElevenLabs dashboard](https://elevenlabs.io/) (voice, personality, knowledge base, tools) and then connect to it at runtime. The adapter wraps the `@elevenlabs/client` SDK for seamless integration with `useRealtimeChat` and `RealtimeClient`.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nvue: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\npreact: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nangular: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\noctane: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependencies:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Server Setup\n\nThe server generates a **signed WebSocket URL** so your API key never reaches the client. The signed URL is valid for 30 minutes.\n\n```typescript group=elevenlabs-1\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\n// In your API route (Express, Hono, TanStack Start, etc.)\nexport async function POST() {\n  const token = await realtimeToken({\n    adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n      agentId: process.env.ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID!,\n    }),\n  })\n\n  return Response.json(token)\n}\n```\n\n### With Overrides\n\nYou can override agent settings at token generation time without changing your dashboard configuration:\n\n```typescript group=elevenlabs-1\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n    agentId: process.env.ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID!,\n    overrides: {\n      voiceId: 'custom-voice-id',\n      systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful voice assistant.',\n      firstMessage: 'Hello! How can I help you today?',\n      language: 'en',\n    },\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n## Client Setup\n\n### React (useRealtimeChat)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nfunction VoiceChat() {\n  const {\n    status,\n    mode,\n    messages,\n    connect,\n    disconnect,\n    pendingUserTranscript,\n    pendingAssistantTranscript,\n    inputLevel,\n    outputLevel,\n  } = useRealtimeChat({\n    getToken: () =>\n      fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n    adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Status: {status}</p>\n      <p>Mode: {mode}</p>\n      <button onClick={status === 'idle' ? connect : disconnect}>\n        {status === 'idle' ? 'Start Conversation' : 'End Conversation'}\n      </button>\n      {pendingUserTranscript && <p>You: {pendingUserTranscript}...</p>}\n      {pendingAssistantTranscript && (\n        <p>AI: {pendingAssistantTranscript}...</p>\n      )}\n      {messages.map((msg) => (\n        <div key={msg.id}>\n          <strong>{msg.role}:</strong>\n          {msg.parts.map((part, i) => (\n            <span key={i}>\n              {part.type === 'text' ? part.content : null}\n              {part.type === 'audio' ? part.transcript : null}\n            </span>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Non-React (RealtimeClient)\n\n```typescript\nimport { RealtimeClient } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst client = new RealtimeClient({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  onMessage: (message) => {\n    console.log(`${message.role}:`, message.parts)\n  },\n  onStatusChange: (status) => {\n    console.log('Status:', status)\n  },\n  onModeChange: (mode) => {\n    console.log('Mode:', mode)\n  },\n})\n\nawait client.connect()\n```\n\n## Client Tools\n\nElevenLabs supports client-side tools that execute in the browser. Define tools using the standard `toolDefinition()` API:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Get weather for a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    conditions: z.string(),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.client(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/weather?location=${location}`)\n  return res.json()\n})\n\n// Pass tools to the hook\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n```\n\nTool results are automatically serialized to strings and returned to the ElevenLabs agent. The adapter converts TanStack tool definitions into the `@elevenlabs/client` clientTools format internally.\n\n## Configuration\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtimeToken` Options\n\nUsed on the **server** to generate a signed WebSocket URL.\n\n| Option | Type | Required | Description |\n|--------|------|----------|-------------|\n| `agentId` | `string` | No\\* | Agent ID configured in the ElevenLabs dashboard. \\*Falls back to `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID`; required only if that env var is unset |\n| `overrides.voiceId` | `string` | No | Custom voice ID to override the agent's default voice |\n| `overrides.systemPrompt` | `string` | No | Custom system prompt to override the agent's default |\n| `overrides.firstMessage` | `string` | No | First message the agent speaks when the session starts |\n| `overrides.language` | `string` | No | Language code (e.g., `'en'`, `'es'`, `'fr'`) |\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtime` Options\n\nUsed on the **client** to establish the connection.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `connectionMode` | `'websocket' \\| 'webrtc'` | auto-detect | Transport protocol for the connection |\n| `debug` | `boolean \\| DebugConfig` | `false` | Enable debug logging — pass `true` for all categories, or a `DebugConfig` to select categories/sink |\n\n## Differences from OpenAI Realtime\n\nElevenLabs and OpenAI take different approaches to realtime voice:\n\n| | ElevenLabs | OpenAI |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Configuration** | Agent-based. Configure voice, personality, and knowledge in the ElevenLabs dashboard or via `overrides` at token time. | Session-based. Configure `instructions`, `voice`, `temperature`, etc. per session via `useRealtimeChat` options. |\n| **Token type** | Signed WebSocket URL (valid 30 minutes) | Ephemeral API token (valid ~10 minutes) |\n| **Transport** | WebSocket (default) or WebRTC | WebRTC |\n| **Audio handling** | `@elevenlabs/client` SDK manages audio capture and playback automatically | TanStack AI manages WebRTC peer connection and audio tracks |\n| **VAD** | Handled by ElevenLabs server-side | Supports `server`, `semantic`, and `manual` modes |\n| **Runtime updates** | Session config is set at creation time and cannot be changed mid-session | Supports `updateSession()` for mid-session config changes |\n| **Image input** | Not supported | Supported via `sendImage()` |\n| **Time domain data** | Not available from the SDK | Available for waveform visualizations |\n\n## Audio Visualization\n\nThe ElevenLabs adapter provides audio visualization data through the same interface as other realtime adapters:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst {\n  inputLevel, // 0-1 normalized microphone volume\n  outputLevel, // 0-1 normalized speaker volume\n  getInputFrequencyData, // Uint8Array frequency spectrum\n  getOutputFrequencyData,\n} = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n})\n```\n\n**Note:** ElevenLabs provides volume levels and frequency data but does not expose time-domain data. The `getInputTimeDomainData()` and `getOutputTimeDomainData()` methods return static placeholder arrays. The default audio sample rate is 16kHz.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet these in your server environment:\n\n```bash\nELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-elevenlabs-api-key\nELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=your-agent-id\n```\n\n| Variable | Required | Description |\n|----------|----------|-------------|\n| `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | Yes | Your ElevenLabs API key, used server-side for generating signed URLs |\n| `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID` | No | Default agent ID. Can also be passed directly to `elevenlabsRealtimeToken()` |\n\nGet your API key from the [ElevenLabs dashboard](https://elevenlabs.io/). Create and configure agents in the **Conversational AI** section of the dashboard.\n\n## Text-to-Speech\n\nFor one-shot speech generation (not realtime), use `elevenlabsSpeech` with `generateSpeech()`:\n\nThe `format` option supports `mp3` (default), `pcm`, `opus`, and `wav`. WAV output contains 44.1 kHz, 16-bit mono PCM with a RIFF header. Requests for `aac` or `flac` throw before the API call. An explicit `modelOptions.outputFormat` overrides `format` and returns the selected provider format without WAV wrapping.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  text: \"Hello from ElevenLabs!\",\n  voice: \"Rachel\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.audio); // Base64-encoded audio\n```\n\n### Dialogue and timings\n\nElevenLabs has a separate dialogue endpoint that takes up to **10 distinct\nvoices**, and a timestamped twin of each endpoint. `turns` and `timestamps`\npick between them, so you never choose an endpoint by hand:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  turns: [\n    { text: \"Knock knock.\", voice: \"bYTqZQo3Jz7LQtmGTgwi\" },\n    { text: \"Who is there?\", voice: \"6lCwbsX1yVjD49QmpkTR\" },\n  ],\n  timestamps: true,\n});\n\n// Character timings for the whole clip.\nconsole.log(result.alignment?.unit); // 'character'\n\n// One entry per turn, with the voice that spoke it.\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.turnIndex, segment.voice, segment.text);\n}\n```\n\n`segments` only comes back from the dialogue endpoint. A single-voice request\nwith `timestamps: true` returns `alignment` alone.\n\n## Music & Sound Effects\n\n`elevenlabsAudio` covers both music generation and sound effects depending on the model:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateAudio } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsAudio } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\n// Music generation\nconst music = await generateAudio({\n  adapter: elevenlabsAudio(\"music_v2_5\"),\n  prompt: \"An upbeat synthwave track for a product launch\",\n});\n\n// Sound effects\nconst sfx = await generateAudio({\n  adapter: elevenlabsAudio(\"eleven_text_to_sound_v2\"),\n  prompt: \"A glass shattering on concrete\",\n});\n```\n\n## Listing Voices\n\n`elevenlabsSpeech` can read the account's voice catalog, which includes anything `generateVoice()` has saved:\n\n```typescript\nimport { listVoices } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst { voices } = await listVoices({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  origins: [\"generated\", \"cloned\"],\n});\n```\n\nElevenLabs has no origin filter on `GET /v1/voices`, so the adapter fetches the catalog and narrows in memory. Its `famous` and `high_quality` categories both read as `professional`.\n\n## Voice Design\n\n`elevenlabsVoiceDesign` creates a new voice from a description. The voice IDs it returns go straight into `generateSpeech()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVoice } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign(\"eleven_ttv_v3\"),\n  prompt: \"A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties with a slight Irish lilt\",\n  name: \"Irish Narrator\",\n});\n\nconst [voice] = result.voices;\nif (!voice) throw new Error(\"The provider returned no voices.\");\n\nconsole.log(voice.voiceId);\nconsole.log(voice.saved); // true, because a name was given\n```\n\nWithout a `name`, you get preview voices to audition. With a `name`, the best candidate is kept in your ElevenLabs voice library.\n\n`eleven_ttv_v3` also accepts `referenceAudio`, a clip of a real speaker used as a design reference — it still needs a `prompt`, and `modelOptions.promptStrength` balances the two. `eleven_multilingual_ttv_v2` takes no reference audio. See [Voice Creation](../media/voice-creation) for the full guide.\n\n## Models\n\n| Family | Models |\n| --- | --- |\n| Text-to-speech | `eleven_v4`, `eleven_v4_turbo`, `eleven_v3`, `eleven_v3_conversational`, `eleven_multilingual_v2`, `eleven_flash_v2_5`, `eleven_flash_v2` |\n| Music | `music_v2_5`, `music_v2` |\n| Sound effects | `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` |\n| Transcription | `scribe_v2`, `scribe_v2_medical` |\n| Voice design | `eleven_ttv_v3`, `eleven_multilingual_ttv_v2` |\n\nElevenLabs deprecated `eleven_turbo_v2`, `eleven_turbo_v2_5`, `eleven_monolingual_v1`, `scribe_v1`, and `music_v1`. The adapter still accepts them, and each is commented as deprecated in `model-meta.ts`. Move to the current model in the same row.\n\n## Transcription\n\nTranscribe audio with `elevenlabsTranscription`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: elevenlabsTranscription(\"scribe_v2\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text);\n```\n\n## Behind a proxy\n\nRoute every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`. These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createElevenLabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst adapter = createElevenLabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\", process.env.ELEVENLABS_API_KEY!, {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/elevenlabs\",\n  defaultHeaders: { \"cf-aig-authorization\": `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});\n```\n\nThis applies to the speech, audio, and transcription adapters. `baseUrl` and `headers` are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtimeToken(options)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs realtime token adapter for server-side use with `realtimeToken()`.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `options.agentId` - Agent ID from the ElevenLabs dashboard\n- `options.overrides?.voiceId` - Custom voice ID\n- `options.overrides?.systemPrompt` - Custom system prompt\n- `options.overrides?.firstMessage` - First message the agent speaks\n- `options.overrides?.language` - Language code\n\n**Returns:** A `RealtimeTokenAdapter` for use with `realtimeToken()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtime(options?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs realtime client adapter for use with `useRealtimeChat` or `RealtimeClient`.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `options.connectionMode?` - `'websocket'` or `'webrtc'` (default: auto-detect)\n- `options.debug?` - Enable debug logging\n\n**Returns:** A `RealtimeAdapter` for use with `useRealtimeChat()` or `RealtimeClient`.\n\n### `elevenlabsSpeech(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs text-to-speech adapter for use with `generateSpeech()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsAudio(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsAudio(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs audio adapter that covers both music generation and sound effects (selected via the model id) for use with `generateAudio()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsTranscription(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs transcription adapter for use with `generateTranscription()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsVoiceDesign(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsVoiceDesign(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs voice-design adapter for use with `generateVoice()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsSpeech(...).listVoices(options?)`\n\nReads the account's voice catalog via `GET /v1/voices`, for use with `listVoices()`.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **No text chat support** -- Use OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or another text adapter for `chat()`.\n- **No summarization** -- Use a text adapter for `summarize()`.\n- **No image input** (realtime) -- ElevenLabs realtime does not support sending images during a conversation.\n- **No runtime session updates** (realtime) -- Session configuration is fixed at connection time.\n- **No time-domain audio data** (realtime) -- Frequency data and volume levels are available, but waveform data is not.\n- **Agent required** (realtime) -- You must create and configure an agent in the ElevenLabs dashboard before using the realtime adapter.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Realtime Voice Chat Guide](../media/realtime-chat) - Complete guide to building realtime voice applications\n- [OpenAI Adapter](./openai) - Alternative realtime voice provider with WebRTC\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: ElevenLabs\nid: elevenlabs-adapter\norder: 9\ndescription: \"Build realtime voice-to-voice conversational AI with ElevenLabs agents in TanStack AI via the @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs adapter.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - elevenlabs\n  - realtime voice ai\n  - conversational ai\n  - voice chat\n  - voice agents\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe ElevenLabs adapter is **voice-focused**. It exposes five capabilities:\n\n- **Realtime voice agents** (`elevenlabsRealtime` / `elevenlabsRealtimeToken`) — full-duplex voice-to-voice conversations powered by ElevenLabs Conversational AI agents.\n- **Text-to-speech** (`elevenlabsSpeech`) — one-shot speech generation via `generateSpeech()`.\n- **Music & sound effects** (`elevenlabsAudio`) — one-shot audio generation via `generateAudio()`.\n- **Transcription** (`elevenlabsTranscription`) — speech-to-text via `generateTranscription()`.\n- **Voice design** (`elevenlabsVoiceDesign`): create a new voice via `generateVoice()`.\n\nIt does not support text `chat()` or `summarize()` — use OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini for those.\n\nThe realtime adapter uses an **agent-based architecture** where you configure your conversational AI agent in the [ElevenLabs dashboard](https://elevenlabs.io/) (voice, personality, knowledge base, tools) and then connect to it at runtime. The adapter wraps the `@elevenlabs/client` SDK for seamless integration with `useRealtimeChat` and `RealtimeClient`.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nvue: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\npreact: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nangular: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\noctane: @tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependencies:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Server Setup\n\nThe server generates a **signed WebSocket URL** so your API key never reaches the client. The signed URL is valid for 30 minutes.\n\n```typescript group=elevenlabs-1\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\n// In your API route (Express, Hono, TanStack Start, etc.)\nexport async function POST() {\n  const token = await realtimeToken({\n    adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n      agentId: process.env.ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID!,\n    }),\n  })\n\n  return Response.json(token)\n}\n```\n\n### With Overrides\n\nYou can override agent settings at token generation time without changing your dashboard configuration:\n\n```typescript group=elevenlabs-1\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n    agentId: process.env.ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID!,\n    overrides: {\n      voiceId: 'custom-voice-id',\n      systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful voice assistant.',\n      firstMessage: 'Hello! How can I help you today?',\n      language: 'en',\n    },\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n## Client Setup\n\n### React (useRealtimeChat)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nfunction VoiceChat() {\n  const {\n    status,\n    mode,\n    messages,\n    connect,\n    disconnect,\n    pendingUserTranscript,\n    pendingAssistantTranscript,\n    inputLevel,\n    outputLevel,\n  } = useRealtimeChat({\n    getToken: () =>\n      fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n    adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Status: {status}</p>\n      <p>Mode: {mode}</p>\n      <button onClick={status === 'idle' ? connect : disconnect}>\n        {status === 'idle' ? 'Start Conversation' : 'End Conversation'}\n      </button>\n      {pendingUserTranscript && <p>You: {pendingUserTranscript}...</p>}\n      {pendingAssistantTranscript && (\n        <p>AI: {pendingAssistantTranscript}...</p>\n      )}\n      {messages.map((msg) => (\n        <div key={msg.id}>\n          <strong>{msg.role}:</strong>\n          {msg.parts.map((part, i) => (\n            <span key={i}>\n              {part.type === 'text' ? part.content : null}\n              {part.type === 'audio' ? part.transcript : null}\n            </span>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Non-React (RealtimeClient)\n\n```typescript\nimport { RealtimeClient } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst client = new RealtimeClient({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  onMessage: (message) => {\n    console.log(`${message.role}:`, message.parts)\n  },\n  onStatusChange: (status) => {\n    console.log('Status:', status)\n  },\n  onModeChange: (mode) => {\n    console.log('Mode:', mode)\n  },\n})\n\nawait client.connect()\n```\n\n## Client Tools\n\nElevenLabs supports client-side tools that execute in the browser. Define tools using the standard `toolDefinition()` API:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Get weather for a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    conditions: z.string(),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.client(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/weather?location=${location}`)\n  return res.json()\n})\n\n// Pass tools to the hook\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n```\n\nTool results are automatically serialized to strings and returned to the ElevenLabs agent. The adapter converts TanStack tool definitions into the `@elevenlabs/client` clientTools format internally.\n\n## Configuration\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtimeToken` Options\n\nUsed on the **server** to generate a signed WebSocket URL.\n\n| Option | Type | Required | Description |\n|--------|------|----------|-------------|\n| `agentId` | `string` | No\\* | Agent ID configured in the ElevenLabs dashboard. \\*Falls back to `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID`; required only if that env var is unset |\n| `overrides.voiceId` | `string` | No | Custom voice ID to override the agent's default voice |\n| `overrides.systemPrompt` | `string` | No | Custom system prompt to override the agent's default |\n| `overrides.firstMessage` | `string` | No | First message the agent speaks when the session starts |\n| `overrides.language` | `string` | No | Language code (e.g., `'en'`, `'es'`, `'fr'`) |\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtime` Options\n\nUsed on the **client** to establish the connection.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `connectionMode` | `'websocket' \\| 'webrtc'` | auto-detect | Transport protocol for the connection |\n| `debug` | `boolean \\| DebugConfig` | `false` | Enable debug logging — pass `true` for all categories, or a `DebugConfig` to select categories/sink |\n\n## Differences from OpenAI Realtime\n\nElevenLabs and OpenAI take different approaches to realtime voice:\n\n| | ElevenLabs | OpenAI |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Configuration** | Agent-based. Configure voice, personality, and knowledge in the ElevenLabs dashboard or via `overrides` at token time. | Session-based. Configure `instructions`, `voice`, `temperature`, etc. per session via `useRealtimeChat` options. |\n| **Token type** | Signed WebSocket URL (valid 30 minutes) | Ephemeral API token (valid ~10 minutes) |\n| **Transport** | WebSocket (default) or WebRTC | WebRTC |\n| **Audio handling** | `@elevenlabs/client` SDK manages audio capture and playback automatically | TanStack AI manages WebRTC peer connection and audio tracks |\n| **VAD** | Handled by ElevenLabs server-side | Supports `server`, `semantic`, and `manual` modes |\n| **Runtime updates** | Session config is set at creation time and cannot be changed mid-session | Supports `updateSession()` for mid-session config changes |\n| **Image input** | Not supported | Supported via `sendImage()` |\n| **Time domain data** | Not available from the SDK | Available for waveform visualizations |\n\n## Audio Visualization\n\nThe ElevenLabs adapter provides audio visualization data through the same interface as other realtime adapters:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst {\n  inputLevel, // 0-1 normalized microphone volume\n  outputLevel, // 0-1 normalized speaker volume\n  getInputFrequencyData, // Uint8Array frequency spectrum\n  getOutputFrequencyData,\n} = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () =>\n    fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then((r) => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n})\n```\n\n**Note:** ElevenLabs provides volume levels and frequency data but does not expose time-domain data. The `getInputTimeDomainData()` and `getOutputTimeDomainData()` methods return static placeholder arrays. The default audio sample rate is 16kHz.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet these in your server environment:\n\n```bash\nELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-elevenlabs-api-key\nELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=your-agent-id\n```\n\n| Variable | Required | Description |\n|----------|----------|-------------|\n| `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | Yes | Your ElevenLabs API key, used server-side for generating signed URLs |\n| `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID` | No | Default agent ID. Can also be passed directly to `elevenlabsRealtimeToken()` |\n\nGet your API key from the [ElevenLabs dashboard](https://elevenlabs.io/). Create and configure agents in the **Conversational AI** section of the dashboard.\n\n## Text-to-Speech\n\nFor one-shot speech generation (not realtime), use `elevenlabsSpeech` with `generateSpeech()`:\n\nThe `format` option supports `mp3` (default), `pcm`, `opus`, and `wav`. WAV output contains 44.1 kHz, 16-bit mono PCM with a RIFF header. Requests for `aac` or `flac` throw before the API call. An explicit `modelOptions.outputFormat` overrides `format` and returns the selected provider format without WAV wrapping.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  text: \"Hello from ElevenLabs!\",\n  voice: \"Rachel\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.audio); // Base64-encoded audio\n```\n\n### Dialogue and timings\n\nElevenLabs has a separate dialogue endpoint that takes up to **10 distinct\nvoices**, and a timestamped twin of each endpoint. `turns` and `timestamps`\npick between them, so you never choose an endpoint by hand:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  turns: [\n    { text: \"Knock knock.\", voice: \"bYTqZQo3Jz7LQtmGTgwi\" },\n    { text: \"Who is there?\", voice: \"6lCwbsX1yVjD49QmpkTR\" },\n  ],\n  timestamps: true,\n});\n\n// Character timings for the whole clip.\nconsole.log(result.alignment?.unit); // 'character'\n\n// One entry per turn, with the voice that spoke it.\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.turnIndex, segment.voice, segment.text);\n}\n```\n\n`segments` only comes back from the dialogue endpoint. A single-voice request\nwith `timestamps: true` returns `alignment` alone.\n\n## Music & Sound Effects\n\n`elevenlabsAudio` covers both music generation and sound effects depending on the model:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateAudio } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsAudio } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\n// Music generation\nconst music = await generateAudio({\n  adapter: elevenlabsAudio(\"music_v2_5\"),\n  prompt: \"An upbeat synthwave track for a product launch\",\n});\n\n// Sound effects\nconst sfx = await generateAudio({\n  adapter: elevenlabsAudio(\"eleven_text_to_sound_v2\"),\n  prompt: \"A glass shattering on concrete\",\n});\n```\n\n## Listing Voices\n\n`elevenlabsSpeech` can read the account's voice catalog, which includes anything `generateVoice()` has saved:\n\n```typescript\nimport { listVoices } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst { voices } = await listVoices({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\"),\n  origins: [\"generated\", \"cloned\"],\n});\n```\n\nElevenLabs has no origin filter on `GET /v1/voices`, so the adapter fetches the catalog and narrows in memory. Its `famous` and `high_quality` categories both read as `professional`.\n\n## Voice Design\n\n`elevenlabsVoiceDesign` creates a new voice from a description. The voice IDs it returns go straight into `generateSpeech()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVoice } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign(\"eleven_ttv_v3\"),\n  prompt: \"A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties with a slight Irish lilt\",\n  name: \"Irish Narrator\",\n});\n\nconst [voice] = result.voices;\nif (!voice) throw new Error(\"The provider returned no voices.\");\n\nconsole.log(voice.voiceId);\nconsole.log(voice.saved); // true, because a name was given\n```\n\nWithout a `name`, you get preview voices to audition. With a `name`, the best candidate is kept in your ElevenLabs voice library.\n\n`eleven_ttv_v3` also accepts `referenceAudio`, a clip of a real speaker used as a design reference — it still needs a `prompt`, and `modelOptions.promptStrength` balances the two. `eleven_multilingual_ttv_v2` takes no reference audio. See [Voice Creation](../media/voice-creation) for the full guide.\n\n## Models\n\n| Family | Models |\n| --- | --- |\n| Text-to-speech | `eleven_v4`, `eleven_v4_turbo`, `eleven_v3`, `eleven_v3_conversational`, `eleven_multilingual_v2`, `eleven_flash_v2_5`, `eleven_flash_v2` |\n| Music | `music_v2_5`, `music_v2` |\n| Sound effects | `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` |\n| Transcription | `scribe_v2`, `scribe_v2_medical` |\n| Voice design | `eleven_ttv_v3`, `eleven_multilingual_ttv_v2` |\n\nElevenLabs deprecated `eleven_turbo_v2`, `eleven_turbo_v2_5`, `eleven_monolingual_v1`, `scribe_v1`, and `music_v1`. The adapter still accepts them, and each is commented as deprecated in `model-meta.ts`. Move to the current model in the same row.\n\n## Transcription\n\nTranscribe audio with `elevenlabsTranscription`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { elevenlabsTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: elevenlabsTranscription(\"scribe_v2\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text);\n```\n\n## Behind a proxy\n\nRoute every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`. These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createElevenLabsSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs\";\n\nconst adapter = createElevenLabsSpeech(\"eleven_v4\", process.env.ELEVENLABS_API_KEY!, {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/elevenlabs\",\n  defaultHeaders: { \"cf-aig-authorization\": `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});\n```\n\nThis applies to the speech, audio, and transcription adapters. `baseUrl` and `headers` are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtimeToken(options)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs realtime token adapter for server-side use with `realtimeToken()`.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `options.agentId` - Agent ID from the ElevenLabs dashboard\n- `options.overrides?.voiceId` - Custom voice ID\n- `options.overrides?.systemPrompt` - Custom system prompt\n- `options.overrides?.firstMessage` - First message the agent speaks\n- `options.overrides?.language` - Language code\n\n**Returns:** A `RealtimeTokenAdapter` for use with `realtimeToken()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsRealtime(options?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs realtime client adapter for use with `useRealtimeChat` or `RealtimeClient`.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `options.connectionMode?` - `'websocket'` or `'webrtc'` (default: auto-detect)\n- `options.debug?` - Enable debug logging\n\n**Returns:** A `RealtimeAdapter` for use with `useRealtimeChat()` or `RealtimeClient`.\n\n### `elevenlabsSpeech(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs text-to-speech adapter for use with `generateSpeech()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsAudio(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsAudio(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs audio adapter that covers both music generation and sound effects (selected via the model id) for use with `generateAudio()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsTranscription(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs transcription adapter for use with `generateTranscription()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsVoiceDesign(model, config?)` / `createElevenLabsVoiceDesign(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an ElevenLabs voice-design adapter for use with `generateVoice()`.\n\n### `elevenlabsSpeech(...).listVoices(options?)`\n\nReads the account's voice catalog via `GET /v1/voices`, for use with `listVoices()`.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **No text chat support** -- Use OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or another text adapter for `chat()`.\n- **No summarization** -- Use a text adapter for `summarize()`.\n- **No image input** (realtime) -- ElevenLabs realtime does not support sending images during a conversation.\n- **No runtime session updates** (realtime) -- Session configuration is fixed at connection time.\n- **No time-domain audio data** (realtime) -- Frequency data and volume levels are available, but waveform data is not.\n- **Agent required** (realtime) -- You must create and configure an agent in the ElevenLabs dashboard before using the realtime adapter.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Realtime Voice Chat Guide](../media/realtime-chat) - Complete guide to building realtime voice applications\n- [OpenAI Adapter](./openai) - Alternative realtime voice provider with WebRTC\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n"}
